  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The versicle and response that close the psalm section and open the confession. It stands as a document of its own because the two texts on either side of it are documents of their own: the psalm before it (ordinarium.iudica-me) is omitted on some days and it is not, and the Confíteor after it is already in the corpus as ordinarium.confiteor. Both witnesses print a cross glyph in the versicle — do after nostrum, handmissal-eo before Adiutórium — a direction for the hand rather than a word; it is stripped, and the disagreement about where to put it is not collated. Neither line has an elliptical verb written out: Adiutórium nostrum in nómine Dómini stands without est.",
    "source": {
      "method": "Verified by collation against the independent witnesses below: zero substantive divergence. The accidental variant is adjudicated in the apparatus.",
